PASS a cue/bin set is audited against its disc DAT, and Organise keeps disc images as they are :: ('Scanned 11 files: 4 new; read 5 files (379 KB).', 1, True)
PASS Convert… turns a cue/bin set into a CHD where it is, sets the originals aside, and the game is still had :: ('chd', '1 game to convert.\n\nConvert: 1 file\n175 KB\n\n3 files are set aside in .gamerepo-set-aside at the top of their folder, until you empty it (History).', 'Converted PlayStation to CHD where they are: 1 of 1 step done.\nUndo\nHistory', ['Disc Game (USA).chd'])
PASS Extract writes a CHD back out as the cue/bin Redump lists, byte for byte :: ('Extracted PlayStation into Extracted: 3 of 3 steps done.\nUndo\nHistory', {'Disc Game (USA) (Track 1).bin': 'f80da677808bc14e543c1564dc3874a134f2c945', 'Disc Game (USA) (Track 2).bin': 'ba3fbcfc61db51f3e970b47675edf92000f937a6', 'Disc Game (USA).cue': 'ea406192c54308382380c44eb84470557b214474'})
PASS Undo puts the extracted files and the CHD's originals back as they were :: (['Disc Game (USA) (Track 1).bin', 'Disc Game (USA) (Track 2).bin', 'Disc Game (USA).cue'], True)
PASS Settings › Preferred formats keeps the platform's choice in the library, and Convert… offers it first :: ({'psp': 'zso'}, ['cso', 'zso', 'chd', 'extract'])
PASS Settings › Tools keeps where dolphin-tool is on this computer, shows what it found, and clears it :: ({'dolphin-tool': 'D:\\a\\Game-Repo\\Game-Repo\\tests\\fixtures\\fake_dolphin_tool.py'}, 'D:\\a\\Game-Repo\\Game-Repo\\tests\\fixtures\\fake_dolphin_tool.py', True)
PASS Settings › Tools has Get it… (a checked download) or the download page for each tool, and no longer says nothing is downloaded (D178) :: ([['dolphin-tool', 'get', 'Get it…'], ['innoextract', 'get', 'Get it…'], ['tesseract', 'page', 'Download page']], "Tools\n\nGame Repo reads and writes CHD, CSO and ZSO itself. For RVZ it uses Dolphin's own tool, and for GOG installers innoextract, found in the app's tools folder (D:\\a\\Game-Repo\\Game-Repo\\desktop\\tar")
PASS Get it… downloads innoextract and dolphin-tool into the tools folder, checks them and shows their SHA-256 (D178) :: ({'innoextract': ['D:\\a\\Game-Repo\\Game-Repo\\desktop\\target\\release\\tools\\innoextract.exe · innoextract 1.9', 'Downloaded 1.9 · SHA-256 6989342c9b026a00a72a38f23b62a8e6a22cc5de69805cf47d68ac2fec993065'], 'dolphin-tool': ['D:\\a\\Game-Repo\\Game-Repo\\desktop\\target\\release\\tools\\DolphinTool.exe', 'Downloaded 2609a · SHA-256 bbfd13bf9e6d2a4164a15c392b1f32a9b18150e5136746b388704608fbb60f76']}, ['DolphinTool.exe', 'Qt6Core.dll', 'Qt6Gui.dll', 'Qt6Svg.dll', 'Qt6Widgets.dll', 'dolphin-tool.json', 'innoextract.exe', 'innoextract.json'])
